# WiFi coexistence (docs/pageflip.md section 6), RIGHT half: an ordinary paired reader, waiting for
# a peer whose radio is suspended. It presses nothing at all -- every page it shows was decided by
# the join and by the other half's press, which is what makes it evidence that the pair re-formed.
log pageflip-wifi-right: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
# The cache build. Nothing can arrive before this: the other half has no radio yet.
wait 9000
# Blocks until the other half releases WiFi, greets, and the join lands. Waiting on it rather than
# sleeping past it is the point -- this is the resume the section is about.
expect peer present
# The Swapped exchange of section 4.2 seeks this half to the other's page, one ahead.
wait 3000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-wifi-right-00.bmp
# The other half presses once around here; this one advances with it, by two.
wait 8000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-wifi-right-01.bmp
wait 1000
log pageflip-wifi-right: done
quit
